Explanation:
To “balance” our overall protection so that we do not “over‐commit” drones to fields which already have a heavy influx (or even zero threat – as is the case for Field_4) we can reassign any drone whose current target is a field that is not one of the allowed protection groups to idle. (Note that in the allowed groups list there is no “protecting Field_4”.) Thus every drone whose target is something that appears in the allowed list (for example, Field_1, Field_2, Field_3, Field_5, Field_6, Field_7, Field_8, Field_9, and Field_68) remains assigned to “protecting Field_X” while all drones headed for Field_4 are set to idle. This is one acceptable answer that meets the assignment requirements.
